# hft3 standing workflow (orchestrator)

Owner standing instruction. Applies to every hft3 task unless the user overrides in-thread.

## Fable mindset (load first)

**First context every session** — see [.cursor/rules/00-fable-mindset.mdc](00-fable-mindset.mdc) (always-on, hardened runtime rule). Vault copy: [docs/vault/FABLE_MINDSET.md](../../docs/vault/FABLE_MINDSET.md). Full reference: `C:\Users\MSI\.codex\skills\fable-mindset\references\Fable_Mindset_public.md`. No vault, graph, or code work before Fable.

## Ponytail mindset (mandatory second)

**Second context every session** — see [.cursor/rules/01-ponytail-mindset.mdc](01-ponytail-mindset.mdc) (always-on, after Fable). Charter: [docs/ai/PONYTAIL.md](../../docs/ai/PONYTAIL.md). Upstream: https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail · Vendored: `vendor/ponytail/`. No code edits before Ponytail.

## Main agent = orchestrator / brain

The **main agent** owns intent, vault/repo grounding, planning, integration, and gate sequencing. It does **not** absorb large implementation inline.

- **Default delegate:** coding implementation goes to **Composer 2.5** (builder / task subagents) unless the user explicitly says otherwise.
- Chain detail: [.cursor/rules/delegate-subagents.mdc](delegate-subagents.mdc)

## Mandatory gates (every code change)

Non-negotiable order — skip none **except graph while waived** (item 3):

0. **Fable mindset** — [.cursor/rules/00-fable-mindset.mdc](00-fable-mindset.mdc) + [docs/vault/FABLE_MINDSET.md](../../docs/vault/FABLE_MINDSET.md). **First** every session.
1. **Ponytail mindset** — [.cursor/rules/01-ponytail-mindset.mdc](01-ponytail-mindset.mdc) + [docs/ai/PONYTAIL.md](../../docs/ai/PONYTAIL.md). **Second** — before codebase.
2. **Vault / Ontology gate** — `scripts/vault_gate.ps1` + `scripts/vault_pre_edit.ps1`; consult Obsidian vault (`wiki/hot.md`, `Home.md`, `Memory Stack.md`, relevant `decisions/`). See [.cursor/rules/graph-before-code.mdc](graph-before-code.mdc).
3. **Graph gates** — While vault `wiki/hot.md` contains `waived-by-owner-2026-06-16`: **skip** GraphGate, GraphPre, GraphPost; VaultGate + targeted reads replace graph. Once owner lifts the waiver: GraphGate + GraphPre before edits and GraphPost after code edits are **mandatory again**.
4. **Plan / locate / implement** — delegate; main thread integrates.
5. **Local preflight** — mandatory bounded task-specific `rg` hygiene for stale terms, old fields, missing rows, and whitespace. This is not GrepLoop.
6. **Dual-pass review** — spawn **cavecrew-reviewer** per [docs/REVIEWER_CHARTER.md](../../docs/REVIEWER_CHARTER.md) (Pass A Karpathy + Pass B math invariants). See [.cursor/rules/reviewer-charter.mdc](reviewer-charter.mdc).
7. **Verify** — bounded pytest/gates with **exact command, exit code, and output tail** pasted in thread.
8. **Plan Drift Review** — compare executed work against the approved plan before Review Surface Gate.
9. **Review Surface Gate** — create or reuse a PR/MR/CL review surface after Plan Drift Review passes when the work is intended to advance toward merge-ready. If blocked, report `pr-ai-review: unavailable(no-pr)` and `merge-ready: no`.
10. **PR GrepLoop** — run the installed external PR AI loop on the current-head review surface. Fix actionable feedback, rerun local gates, push, and repeat until clean or bounded stop. Missing connector/auth means `merge-ready: no` unless the owner explicitly records `pr-ai-review: waived-by-user` plus `review-surface: none(waived-by-user: <reason>)`.
11. **Validation honesty handoff** — status block per [docs/VALIDATION_HONESTY.md](../../docs/VALIDATION_HONESTY.md). See [.cursor/rules/validation-honesty.mdc](validation-honesty.mdc).

## Optional / contrast gates

- **Local grep / preflight** — mandatory hygiene, but do **not** label local `rg` searches **"GrepLoop"** (reserved for external PR/MR/CL AI review connectors).
- **External PR/MR/CL review connector loops** and **reviewer-finding loops** remain mandatory until **0 🔴** or user explicitly accepts/waives. Do not claim merge-ready while open 🔴 remain.
